=begin

Attempts to cast non-attack spells from your collection of scrolls,
vellums, parchments, etc. Utilizes separate containers to manage vibrant scrolls.

Reads every scroll ONCE up front -- your reserve slots, your scrollsack, and your
vibrantscrollsack -- silently (no game spam), prints what it found that matches the
spells you asked for, then invokes only those specific scrolls.

Reserve scrolls are invoked directly by id (no need to hold them). Container scrolls
are picked up, invoked, and put back. Vibrant scrolls are skipped unless the vibrant
toggle is on, in which case their spell knowledge is absorbed and incanted up to the
spell's maximum duration.

Invoke/casts normal scrolls.
Incants spells absorbed from vibrant scrolls.

Originally based on the work by Sulien on scrollbuff.lic, this script has been
almost entirely re-written to allow:
Invoking from either hand,
Support for vibrant ink scrolls,
Support for reserved scrolls,
Support for self-cast utility spells,
Configurable durations for stackable or refreshable spells

    author: Nihiladrem (todd.estabrooks@gmail.com)
      game: gs
      tags: invoke, scroll, scrolls, hunting
      version: 0.2.0

    CHANGELOG:
    0.2.0 - Reworked to scan once instead of probing per spell. Old flow looped over
            every requested spell and, for each, invoke-tested both reserve scrolls
            then rummaged both containers -- dozens of "That spell is not on the ..."
            and failed-rummage lines. New flow reads every candidate scroll a single
            time (same silent Lich::Util.issue_command read that scrollinv.lic uses),
            builds a spell -> scroll map, then invokes only the specific scrolls
            chosen. A scroll carrying several requested spells is picked up once and
            invoked for each. findscroll/castscroll replaced by read_spell_pairs /
            scroll_contents / invoke_and_cast.
            Quiet by default now: this script's own command echoes
            ([scrollbuff3]>invoke ...) are hidden for the whole run via
            Script.current.silent, cutting the noise from the old per-spell probing
            without hiding the game's own responses to each cast, so you can still
            see what's being cast. ;scrollbuff3 verbose un-hides the echoes too and
            adds a SCROLL SCAN table; ;scrollbuff3 quiet reverts.
    0.1.14 - 0.1.13's reserve check re-tested every reserve item against every spell
             number, even ones already matched to a different spell -- spammy with a
             couple of reserve items and a long spell list (e.g. one item matched to
             spell 211, then re-tried and failing against every other spell requested
             after it). A reserve item's spell doesn't change during a run, so matches
             are now cached and reused instead of re-tested.
    0.1.13 - Added support for scrolls sitting in reserve slots (see ;reserve list) --
             these are invoked directly by id and never need to be picked up or put
             away. findscroll now checks reserve before rummaging any container, and
             returns [scrolltype, scrollid] (plus an already-completed invoke result
             for reserve hits, so castscroll doesn't invoke it twice) instead of
             leaving the caller to guess scrollid from checkright/checkleft -- which
             also fixes findscroll silently returning nil when vibrant use was toggled
             on and the very first rummage already found a normal (non-vibrant) scroll.
             The "That spell is not on the ..." retry in castscroll now also figures
             out which hand (if any) actually holds the failed scroll instead of
             assuming it's always in the right hand.
    0.1.12 - The 0.1.9 "no progress" cap check read timeleft right after casting, before
             the duration feed had caught up, so it mistook a normal update lag for
             hitting the real cap: it broke out of the incant loop early, then the outer
             loop re-invoked from the now-empty vibrant scroll ("That spell is not on
             the ..."), which put it in the wrong sack (always scrollsack, regardless of
             where it came from) and could try to put it away a second time at the end.
             The cap check now waits up to 3 seconds for the duration to update, the
             retry puts the scroll back in the sack matching its scrolltype, and the
             final put-away is skipped if the scroll isn't actually in a hand anymore.
    0.1.11 - Renamed the scrollbag/vibrantscrollbag vars to scrollsack/vibrantscrollsack
             to match the container vars used by fizzfuse.lic. Still set with
             ;vars set scrollsack=... and ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=...
    0.1.10 - Fixed the help/settings display always showing "Use vibrant Scrolls: No"
             regardless of the actual toggle: it compared scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle
             to "Yes", but the setting is stored as "True"/"False" everywhere else in
             the script.
    0.1.9 - Fixed infinite incant loop introduced in 0.1.8: the stacking loop compared
            timeleft > target_duration, but a spell can never exceed its own server-
            enforced cap, so once it reached max it looped forever (seen with 905
            stuck at its 4h10m cap). Comparisons now use >=, and as a second safety
            net the loop also stops if an incant doesn't actually add duration, in
            case the real server cap differs from the spell's declared max.
    0.1.8 - Vibrant ink scrolls grant temporary knowledge of the spell instead of
            consuming a scroll per cast, so stackable spells cast from a vibrant
            scroll now stack up to the spell's real maximum duration instead of
            stopping at stackto_duration. Refreshable and one-shot spells are
            unaffected since recasting them doesn't add duration.
    0.1.7 - Stopped findscroll from mutating SpellNumsNeeded with .shift, which removed
            the wrong spell (whatever was first in the list) whenever any scroll was
            missing, mislabeling successfully-cast spells as skipped. Final summary now
            separately lists spells cast, spells whose scroll wasn't found, and spells
            that weren't needed.
    0.1.6 - Fixed active-spell detection to use Spell.active/active? (like ewaggle.lic)
            instead of the raw spell.active attribute, and to compare each spell's
            remaining duration against the correct threshold for its type
            (stackable/refreshable/one-shot) instead of always using stackto.
    0.1.5 - Fixed an issue with scrolls being stored incorrectly in vibrantscrollsack
    0.1.4 - Fixed a bug with vibrant scroll casting
    0.1.3 - Changed logic to allow all non-attack spells.
    0.1.2 - Changed vars to scrollbag to avoid confusion, clarified help messaging.
    0.1.1 - Scrollbuff2 rework by Nihiladrem
    0.0.1 - Initial version by Sulien
    
=end

debug = false

def echofmt(*lines)
    maxlen = lines.map(&:length).max + 1
    echo "=" * maxlen
    lines.each do |line|
        echo line + (" " * (maxlen - line.length))
    end
    echo "=" * maxlen
end

##Check for empty hand
unless (checkright.nil?) ||  (checkleft.nil?)
    echofmt "Empty a hand and try again"
    exit
end

##Check for scrollsack
scrollsackVar = Vars["scrollsack"]
unless scrollsackVar
    echofmt "Please set your scroll container with a",
            "command like:",
            "    ;vars set scrollsack=silver backpack",
            "",
            "Use only a noun and optionally a single adjective.",
            "",
            "This will only work with containers you are",
            "wearing or holding."
    
    exit
end
scrollsack = GameObj[scrollsackVar]
unless scrollsack
    echofmt "Couldn't find your scrollsack \"#{scrollsackVar}\"",
            "Fetch that and try again, would ya?"
    
    exit
end
##Check for vibrantscrollsack
vibrantscrollsackVar = Vars["vibrantscrollsack"]
unless vibrantscrollsackVar
    echofmt "Please set your vibrant scroll container with a",
            "command like:",
            "    ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=white satchel",
            "",
            "Use only a noun and optionally a single adjective.",
            "",
            "This will only work with containers you are",
            "wearing or holding.",
			"",
			"Your vibrantscrollsack needs to be a different",
			"than your scrollsack."
    exit
end

##Get duration settings
stackto_duration = CharSettings["scrollbuff-stackto"]
if debug == true; echo "Stack duration: #{stackto_duration}";end
if !(CharSettings["scrollbuff-stackto"].to_i > 0)
	if debug == true; echo "Warning! No stackto value set using default of 90 minutes.";end
	stackto_duration = 90
end
refreshto_duration = CharSettings["scrollbuff-refreshto"]
if debug == true;echo "Refresh duration: #{refreshto_duration}";end
if !(CharSettings["scrollbuff-refreshto"].to_i > 0)
	if debug == true; echo "Warning! No refreshto value set using default of 10 minutes.";end
	refreshto_duration = 10
end

## Verbosity. Quiet by default: only the final summary (and this script's own
## command echoes hidden). `;scrollbuff3 verbose` adds a SCROLL SCAN table of
## every scroll and which requested spell it matches, and un-hides the echoes;
## `;scrollbuff3 quiet` reverts.
verbose = (CharSettings["scrollbuff-verbose"] == "True")

##Check for script commands
SpellNums = script.vars[1..-1]
if SpellNums.nil? || SpellNums.count == 0 || SpellNums.first.start_with?("h")
    echofmt "Attempts to cast defensive or self-cast spells from your collection of scrolls, vellums, parchments, etc.",
			"Reads every scroll once -- reserve slots, scrollsack, and vibrantscrollsack -- works out",
			"which scrolls carry the spells you asked for, then invokes only those. Reserve scrolls are",
			"invoked in place; container scrolls are picked up, invoked, and put back.",
            "",
            "Before running, you must set your scrollsack and vibrantscrollsack with a command like:",
            "   ;vars set scrollsack=pouch",
            "   ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=black satchel",
            "",
			"You must have an empty right hand, or a non-scroll item in right hand and an empty left hand.",
            "",
			"The script will tell you which spells it cast and which it skipped.",
            "Casts stackable spells that are not running or have under",
            "#{stackto_duration} minutes left.  To change this setting enter:",
			"   ;#{script.name} stackto (minutes)",
            "",	
            "Casts refreshable spells that are not running or have under",
            "#{refreshto_duration} minutes left.  To change this setting enter:",
			"   ;#{script.name} refreshto (minutes)",
            "",				
			"Vibrant ink scrolls are skipped unless the vibrant toggle is on. Non-vibrant scrolls are",
			"preferred over vibrant ones, and reserve over containers, when more than one carries a spell.",
			"To toggle use of vibrant ink scrolls enter: ",
			"   ;#{script.name} vibrant",
            "",
			"By default the scan is silent and this script's own command echoes are hidden,",
			"but you'll still see the game's response to each spell actually cast. For a full",
			"SCROLL SCAN table of every scroll and which requested spell it matches:",
			"   ;#{script.name} verbose      (and ;#{script.name} quiet to turn it back off)",
            "",
            "Usage: ;#{script.name} 101 107 509 ...",
            "List up to 30 spell numbers separated by a space.",
            "",
			"To list all relevant settings for this script:",
			"Current settings:"
			
			if (CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] == "True");usevibrant="True";else;usevibrant="No";end
			vmode = (CharSettings["scrollbuff-verbose"] == "True") ? "Verbose" : "Quiet"
			echofmt "scrollsack: #{Vars["scrollsack"]}",
			"Vibrantscrollsack: #{Vars["vibrantscrollsack"]}",	
			"Use vibrant Scrolls: #{usevibrant}",	
			"Stack spells to: #{stackto_duration} minutes",
			"Refresh spells below: #{refreshto_duration} minutes",
			"Output: #{vmode}"


    exit
elsif SpellNums.first.start_with?("vibrant")
	if CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] == "True"
		CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] = "False"
		echofmt "You are now set to NOT use vibrant ink scrolls.",
		"If a vibrant ink scroll is rummaged this script will put the scroll in your vibrantscrollsack and rummage again."
	else
		CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] = "True"
		echofmt "You are now set to use vibrant ink scrolls.",
		"If a vibrant ink scroll is rummaged this script will invoke it to absorb the spell's",
		"knowledge, then incant stackable spells until they hit their maximum duration",
		"(refreshable and one-shot spells are still just cast once)."
	end
	exit
elsif SpellNums.first.start_with?("verbose")
	CharSettings["scrollbuff-verbose"] = "True"
	echofmt "scrollbuff3 is now VERBOSE: it prints a SCROLL SCAN table of every scroll and which requested spell it matches."
	exit
elsif SpellNums.first.start_with?("quiet")
	CharSettings["scrollbuff-verbose"] = "False"
	echofmt "scrollbuff3 is now QUIET: it scans silently and prints only the final summary."
	exit
elsif SpellNums.first.start_with?("stackto")
		if debug == true; echo "Second value: #{SpellNums[1]}";end
		if !(SpellNums[1].to_i > 0)
			echofmt "You need to specify a duration in minutes like:",
			"   ;#{script.name} stackto 30"	
			exit
		end
		CharSettings["scrollbuff-stackto"] = SpellNums[1]
		echofmt "You are now set invoke stackable spells until above #{SpellNums[1]} minutes." 
		exit
elsif SpellNums.first.start_with?("refreshto")
		if debug == true; echo "Second value: #{SpellNums[1]}";end
		if !(SpellNums[1].to_i > 0)
			echofmt "You need to specify a duration in minutes like:",
			"   ;#{script.name} refreshto 5"	
			exit
		end
		CharSettings["scrollbuff-refreshto"] = SpellNums[1]
		echofmt "You are now set invoke stackable spells until above #{SpellNums[1]} minutes." 
		exit		
elsif SpellNums.first.start_with?("settings")
	if (CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] == "True");usevibrant="True";else;usevibrant="No";end
	vmode = (CharSettings["scrollbuff-verbose"] == "True") ? "Verbose" : "Quiet"

	
	echofmt "scrollsack: #{Vars["scrollsack"]}",
			"Vibrantscrollsack: #{Vars["vibrantscrollsack"]}",	
			"Use vibrant Scrolls: #{usevibrant}",	
			"Stack spells to: #{stackto_duration} minutes",
			"Refresh spells below: #{refreshto_duration} minutes",
			"Output: #{vmode}"

	exit			
end

##Check for Vibrant Scroll Sack
vibrantscrollsackVar = Vars["vibrantscrollsack"]
unless (vibrantscrollsackVar || (CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] == "True"))
    echofmt "You are not currently set to use vibrant ink scrolls.",
            "You need to set a place to store vibrant ink scrolls that are rummaged from your scrollsack.",
            "command like:",
            "    ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=black backpack"
    
    exit
else
	vibrantscrollsack = GameObj[vibrantscrollsackVar]
	unless vibrantscrollsack
		echofmt "Couldn't find your vibrantscrollsack \"#{vibrantscrollsack}\"",
				"Fetch that and try again, would ya?"
		exit
	end
	if GameObj[vibrantscrollsackVar] == GameObj[scrollsackVar]
		echofmt "Your vibrantscrollsack must be a different container than your scrollsack",
				"Change one of the other to a different container and try again. Example:",
				"    ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=black backpack",
				"OR",
				"    ;vars set scrollsack=pouch"	
				exit
	end	
end


##Check list of spells for useability
## Use Spell.active (which relies on the self-healing active? check, same as ewaggle.lic)
## rather than the raw spell.active attribute, which can go stale.
active_spell_times = Hash[Spell.active.map { |s| [s.num.to_s, s.timeleft] }]

SpellNumsNeeded = SpellNums.find_all do |spell_num|
    spell = Spell[spell_num]
	if debug == true; echo "Availbility: #{spell.availability}";end
	next false unless spell && !(spell.type =~ /attack/)

	existing_duration = active_spell_times[spell.num.to_s] || 0
	if debug == true; echo "#{spell_num} existing duration: #{existing_duration}";end

	if spell.stackable?
		existing_duration <= stackto_duration.to_f
	elsif spell.refreshable?
		existing_duration <= refreshto_duration.to_f
	else
		existing_duration.zero?
	end
end

if SpellNumsNeeded.count.zero?
    echofmt "NO SPELLS NEEDED",
            "",
            "All spells are active with at least #{stackto_duration} minutes remaining."
    
    exit
end

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Scan phase -- read every candidate scroll ONCE, silently, and build a map of
## spell number => the scrolls that carry it. No per-spell trial-and-error.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Quiet mode (default): hide this script's own command echoes
## ([scrollbuff3]>invoke ...) for the whole scan + cast. The game's own
## responses to those commands (the actual "you feel more confident" /
## "Cast Roundtime" messages) still show, so you can see what's being cast.
## `;#{script.name} verbose` also un-hides the command echoes and adds a
## SCROLL SCAN table.
Script.current.silent = true unless verbose

SCROLL_NOUN_RE = /\b(?:scroll|vellum|parchment|papyrus|palimpsest|paper)\b/i

## Same read-parse approach as scrollinv.lic: issue "read" through
## Lich::Util.issue_command so nothing hits the game window, then pull the
## "(NNN) Spell Name" lines out of the response.
READ_START_RE = /^(?:It takes you a moment to focus on|You continue to read|On the .* you see|You (?:don't|do not) see|There isn't any|nothing (?:scrawled|written|inscribed)|cannot be read|too dark to read|can't make out|You are unable to read)/i

def read_spell_pairs(command)
  waitrt?
  lines = Lich::Util.issue_command(
    command, READ_START_RE, /<prompt/,
    include_end: false, timeout: 4, silent: true, usexml: true, quiet: true
  )
  waitrt?
  pairs = []
  lines.each do |line|
    clean = line.gsub(/<\/?[^>]*>/, "")
    pairs << [$1.to_i, $2.strip] if clean =~ /\((\d+)\)\s+(.*?)\s*$/
  end
  pairs
rescue StandardError
  []
end

## Returns [ [spell numbers], vibrant? ] for one candidate scroll. Reserved
## scrolls are read by id first and by name as a fallback (some reserve items
## don't resolve by "#id").
def scroll_contents(cand)
  pairs = read_spell_pairs("read ##{cand[:id]}")
  if pairs.empty? && cand[:loc] == :reserve
    noun = cand[:name].to_s.sub(/\A(?:a|an|some)\s+/i, "").strip
    pairs = read_spell_pairs("read #{noun}") unless noun.empty?
  end
  [pairs.map(&:first).uniq, pairs.any? { |_n, nm| nm =~ /vibrant\s+ink/i }]
end

use_vibrant = (CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] == "True")

fput "open ##{scrollsack.id}"
fput "open ##{vibrantscrollsack.id}"
[scrollsackVar, vibrantscrollsackVar].compact.uniq.each do |noun|
  Lich::Util.issue_command("look in my #{noun}", /(?:In|Inside) the|There (?:is|are)|That is (?:closed|empty)|don't see|could not find/i, /<prompt/, silent: true, quiet: true, timeout: 5) rescue nil
end
if GameObj.reserve.nil?
  fput "reserve list"
  30.times { break unless GameObj.reserve.nil?; sleep 0.1 }
end

candidates = []
GameObj.reserve.to_a.each do |o|
  candidates << { id: o.id, name: o.name, loc: :reserve } if "#{o.noun} #{o.name}" =~ SCROLL_NOUN_RE
end
Array(GameObj.containers[scrollsack.id]).each do |o|
  candidates << { id: o.id, name: o.name, loc: :scrollsack } if o.noun.to_s =~ SCROLL_NOUN_RE
end
Array(GameObj.containers[vibrantscrollsack.id]).each do |o|
  candidates << { id: o.id, name: o.name, loc: :vibrantscrollsack } if o.noun.to_s =~ SCROLL_NOUN_RE
end

if candidates.empty?
  echofmt "No scrolls found in reserve, #{scrollsackVar}, or #{vibrantscrollsackVar}."
  exit
end

echo "scrollbuff3: reading #{candidates.size} scroll(s)..." if verbose || candidates.size > 6

sources     = Hash.new { |h, k| h[k] = [] }   # spell num (Integer) => [candidate, ...]
needed_ints = SpellNumsNeeded.map(&:to_i)
usable      = proc { |c| c[:loc] == :reserve || !c[:vibrant] || use_vibrant }

candidates.each do |c|
  nums, vibrant = scroll_contents(c)
  c[:vibrant] = vibrant
  c[:spells]  = nums
  nums.each { |n| sources[n] << c }
  break if needed_ints.all? { |n| sources[n].any?(&usable) }
end

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Plan phase -- pick one scroll per needed spell and report what was found.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

LOC_PRIORITY = { reserve: 0, scrollsack: 1, vibrantscrollsack: 2 }.freeze

plan    = []   # [ [spell_num_string, candidate], ... ]
missing = []
report  = []

SpellNumsNeeded.each do |spell_num|
  opts = sources[spell_num.to_i].select(&usable)
  if opts.empty?
    missing << spell_num
    note = sources[spell_num.to_i].any? ? "vibrant only (toggle off)" : "no scroll found"
    report << "  #{spell_num} #{Spell[spell_num].name}: #{note}"
    next
  end
  best = opts.min_by { |c| [LOC_PRIORITY[c[:loc]], c[:vibrant] ? 1 : 0] }
  plan << [spell_num, best]
  tags = [best[:loc].to_s]
  tags << "vibrant" if best[:vibrant]
  report << "  #{spell_num} #{Spell[spell_num].name}: #{best[:name]} (#{tags.join(', ')})"
end

echofmt("SCROLL SCAN", "", *report) if verbose

if plan.empty?
  nn = SpellNums - SpellNumsNeeded
  lines = ["SCROLL BUFFS COMPLETE", "", "Cast: (none)"]
  lines << "No scroll: #{missing.uniq.join(' ')}"                unless missing.empty?
  lines << "Already up / not needed: #{nn.join(' ')}"           unless nn.empty?
  echofmt(*lines)
  exit
end

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Cast phase -- only touch the specific scrolls chosen above.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def hand_holding(id)
  return :right if GameObj.right_hand.id == id
  return :left  if GameObj.left_hand.id == id
  nil
end

def invoke_and_cast(spell_num, id, vibrant, stackto_duration, refreshto_duration)
  spell = Spell[spell_num]

  if spell.stackable?
    ## vibrant scrolls are free to re-incant, so stack them to the spell's real
    ## cap; ordinary/reserve scrolls only stack to the configured stackto.
    target = stackto_duration.to_f
    target = [spell.max_duration.to_f, target].max if vibrant
    return true if spell.timeleft >= target
  elsif spell.refreshable?
    target = nil
    return true if spell.timeleft >= refreshto_duration.to_f
  else
    target = nil
    return true if spell.active?
  end

  did = false
  invoke_re = /ink leaps from the page and seeps into your skin|and gesture to invoke the|That spell is not on the|Invoke from what|You don't have|no more prepared|can't quite recall|unable to/i

  loop do
    break if did && target.nil?                 # non-stacking: one cast is enough
    break if target && spell.timeleft >= target

    waitcastrt?
    waitrt?
    prev = spell.timeleft
    result = dothistimeout "invoke #{spell_num} from ##{id}", 8, invoke_re

    if result =~ /and gesture to invoke the/
      fput "cast"
      did = true
      waitcastrt?
      waitrt?
    elsif result =~ /ink leaps from the page and seeps into your skin/
      ## Vibrant: temporary knowledge granted -- incant at least once, and up
      ## to target if the spell stacks.
      loop do
        unless spell.affordable?
          echo "scrollbuff3: waiting for mana to incant #{spell_num}..."
          wait_until { spell.affordable? }
        end
        waitcastrt?
        waitrt?
        p2 = spell.timeleft
        fput "incant #{spell_num}"
        did = true
        waitcastrt?
        waitrt?
        break if target.nil?
        break if spell.timeleft >= target
        ## The duration feed can lag the cast confirmation -- give it a few
        ## seconds before concluding the spell is capped.
        moved = false
        6.times { break if (moved = spell.timeleft > p2 + 0.5); sleep 0.5 }
        break unless moved
      end
      break
    else
      break   # "That spell is not on the ...", out of charges, timeout, etc.
    end

    next if target.nil?
    moved = false
    6.times { break if (moved = spell.timeleft > prev + 0.5); sleep 0.5 }
    break unless moved
  end

  did
end

cast_ok   = []
cast_fail = []

plan.group_by { |(_sn, c)| c[:id] }.each do |id, entries|
  c       = entries.first[1]
  reserve = (c[:loc] == :reserve)

  unless reserve
    fput "get ##{id}"
    unless hand_holding(id)
      echo "scrollbuff3: couldn't retrieve #{c[:name]}; skipping #{entries.map { |e| e[0] }.join(' ')}."
      entries.each { |sn, _| cast_fail << sn }
      next
    end
  end

  entries.each do |spell_num, _c|
    ok = invoke_and_cast(spell_num, id, c[:vibrant], stackto_duration, refreshto_duration)
    (ok ? cast_ok : cast_fail) << spell_num
  end

  unless reserve
    dest = c[:vibrant] ? vibrantscrollsack.id : scrollsack.id
    h = hand_holding(id)
    fput "put #{h} in ##{dest}" if h
  end
end

##fput "close ##{scrollsack.id}"
##fput "close ##{vibrantscrollsack.id}"

summary = ["SCROLL BUFFS COMPLETE", ""]
summary << "Cast: #{cast_ok.uniq.join(' ')}"                        unless cast_ok.empty?
summary << "Scroll found but not cast: #{cast_fail.uniq.join(' ')}" unless cast_fail.empty?
summary << "No scroll: #{missing.uniq.join(' ')}"                   unless missing.empty?
not_needed = SpellNums - SpellNumsNeeded
summary << "Already up / not needed: #{not_needed.join(' ')}"       unless not_needed.empty?
echofmt(*summary)
